Package: sblreg
Type: Package
Title: Symmetric Bilinear Regression for Signal Subgraph Estimation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Sagnik", "Bhadury", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "sagnikbhadury@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Regression of a scalar outcome on a network (symmetric matrix) predictor with the L1-penalised symmetric
    bilinear model of Wang, Zhang and Dunson (2019) <doi:10.1109/TSP.2019.2899818>. Each nonzero component selects a small
    clique of nodes whose connections relate to the outcome. Provides the coordinate-descent fit (C++), penalty paths,
    cross-validated tuning, a nested cross-validation assessment with a permuted-outcome control, edge and node summaries,
    and the simulation design of the paper.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0)
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.0.0), stats, utils
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
URL: https://github.com/sagnikbhadury/sblreg
